> I know it's recommended to have ?oGD to detect the magic portal on the
> Planes, but of what BUC?  I always thought it was supposed to be
> cursed, but I think I've gotten confused somewhere.  What are the
> differences between the cursed and non-cursed when confused?

confused & uncursed = show traps on map as their true symbol

pro: you can identify portal traps from fire traps by their color.
Great for the plane of fire.

con: you have to get confused. There are safe ways to do this, and
unsafe. !oConfusion is great. having a unknown spell will randomly
stun & confuse you, you can apply unicorn horn & retry to eventually
just get confused. This may take a couple turns. Eating some foods
(tripe rations) can make you confused also.


cursed = show traps as $ on map

pro: no turns wasted on trying to get yourself confused

con: all traps show up as a $ on the map - if there are many traps
(plane of fire) then you won't know which ones are fire traps and
which one is the magic portal "trap".

so generally: i carry 3+ cursed gold detection, and 1 uncursed gold
detection, and 1 potion of confusion. Sometimes cursed gold detection
can be hard to come by, so i substitute as necessary.

